27:["$","p","Check course content, location, accommodation arrangements, total costs and the support you would use. A comfortable offer label does not replace those comparisons. Where an offer changes if you accept it firmly, understand the consequences before responding.",{"children":"Check course content, location, accommodation arrangements, total costs and the support you would use. A comfortable offer label does not replace those comparisons. Where an offer changes if you accept it firmly, understand the consequences before responding."}]
28:["$","p","UCAS explains that accepting an unconditional offer as your firm choice means you cannot make an insurance choice. Check current reply guidance and the options shown in your account; do not use a single universal reply date from an older article.",{"children":"UCAS explains that accepting an unconditional offer as your firm choice means you cannot make an insurance choice. Check current reply guidance and the options shown in your account; do not use a single universal reply date from an older article."}]
29:["$","$L2b",null,{"id":"guides/conditional-vs-unconditional-offer:section-4","title":"Check your progress","items":["All academic conditions copied accurately.","Remaining checks and evidence identified.","Course and practical fit compared.","Actual reply deadline recorded.","Effect on firm/insurance choices understood."]}]
2a:["$","section","4-If results or circumstances change",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-5","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"If results or circumstances change"}],[["$","p","Use the official application status and the university response to decide your next step. If you have missed a condition, contact admissions with the exact result. If an application is unsuccessful or withdrawn, UCAS describes other routes that may be available, but eligibility and dates depend on your position.",{"children":"Use the official application status and the university response to decide your next step. If you have missed a condition, contact admissions with the exact result. If an application is unsuccessful or withdrawn, UCAS describes other routes that may be available, but eligibility and dates depend on your position."}],["$","p","Avoid changing a firm decision simply to remove uncertainty without understanding the alternative. Keep written guidance and reply through the official application route. This guide explains the decision process; it does not accept, decline or amend an offer for you.",{"children":"Avoid changing a firm decision simply to remove uncertainty without understanding the alternative. Keep written guidance and reply through the official application route. This guide explains the decision process; it does not accept, decline or amend an offer for you."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}]
